# issues/fixed/safe-code-reaches-freed-memory-through-arraylist-set-len.md:
# growing an ArrayList over memory it did not write needs the spare-capacity
# token, and a SAFE file (no pragma(Pragma.AllowUnsafe)) cannot hold it: the
# token is an Option(*(T)), a raw pointer VALUE, which the safe-mode value gate
# rejects even when it is discarded (`_ := ...`). The kept substring is that
# gate's own diagnostic, naming the token's type.
stdout_keep_match=Raw pointer values are not available in safe code: '[^']*' has type '[^']*'
timeout=120
